==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
1580, from {{etyl|ang}} dialectical {{term|wiðer||against|lang=ang}} {{suffix||s}}; see {{term|with|lang=en}}. So-named because the part of the horse that pushes ''against'' a load. Compare {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Widerrist||withers|lang=de}} from {{term|wider||against|lang=de}} + {{term|Rist||wrist|lang=de}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈwɪð.ɜː(ɹ)z/}}, {{SAMPA|/"wID.3:(r\)z/}}

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun}}

# {{context|veterinary medicine}} The part of the [[back]] of a [[draft]] [[animal]] or [[horse]] that is the [[highest]], between the [[shoulder blades]].

====Usage notes====
Although this noun refers to one object, there is no corresponding singular form *{{term||wither}} for this word, the singular form being obsolete.

